--- title
# Eviz

--- body
Digital business cards and public pages linked to lead capture and relationship management.

--- actions
[Product website](https://www.eviz.me/) · [All products](/en/#products)
:::

::: section topic-1
## From publishing to CRM

A public business card or landing page is one end of a longer process. A visitor opens the page, follows a contact action or submits a form; the resulting information enters a workflow where it can be organized and followed up. Eviz treats publishing and relationship management as parts of that same product.

The experience therefore spans two very different contexts: public content intended for visitors and authenticated tools used by the account owner.
:::

::: section topic-2
## Application boundaries

Page presentation, lead collection, contact history and commercial records are separate concerns. A shared application model makes it possible to connect them without requiring every feature to know the details of the others.

A modular SaaS application is a practical choice here. Splitting every capability into an independently deployed service could add operational complexity before there is evidence that the individual workloads require it.
:::

::: section topic-3
## Data and verification

The important properties are correct ownership of business records, predictable publication behavior and reliable transfer of information from public forms to the working CRM. Those properties require more than isolated component tests.

The reviewed code contains tests for selected application modules. Complete end-to-end coverage of publication, commercial processing and contact workflows has not been established by this review.
:::

